fix(graph): seed [:HAS_MEMBER] not [:MEMBER_OF] — the on-call join was a phantom edge

The seeder wrote (:Person)-[:MEMBER_OF]->(:Team), but every consumer —
getServiceOwnership, page_on_call, the README ER diagram and the schema — joins
on (:Team)-[:HAS_MEMBER]->(:Person). Nothing ever created HAS_MEMBER, so the
flagship question "who should I page?" resolved no on-call engineer and rendered
"unassigned", and the ownership roster came back empty. Only the seeder was
wrong; the queries were right.

Why no test caught it: the existing verify check asserted the owner team and the
on-call list (both reached via OWNED_BY / ONCALL_FOR) but never the member list,
which is the one edge that was broken.

- seed [:HAS_MEMBER]; docs/GRAPH-MODEL drop the stray MEMBER_OF row
- schema.ts: fix stale IN_CLUSTER (real edge is RUNS_IN), drop never-written
  placeholder types, export canonical REL_TYPES
- tests/graph-contract.test.ts: reads Cypher from source and fails if any
  traversed relationship type is never created (proven to fail on the old seed)
- verify.ts: assert the ownership roster is non-empty, that the on-call chain
  resolves to Priya Nair, and that the answer never says "unassigned"

Also make two other documented-but-unwritten claims real:
- [:WROTE] AgentRun->Memory is now written (runId was a dead parameter); page/
  create/resolve memories link to their run
- [:TOUCHES] matches by name OR id, so trace steps link incidents/documents too
  (was name-only, so they never appeared in the replay highlight)

Harden POST /api/agent: 600-char question cap, bounded/sanitized tenant id.
